@@ -741,3 +741,39 @@ was deleted and the case was watched turning from PASS into a **named** CANNOT
 DETERMINE — not vanishing silently from the case list — and restored.
 `tests/test_discipline_decoupling.py` is that proof, and a check nobody has
 watched fail is not a check.
+
+## Withdrawing a positive claim — demotion only (2026-09-08)
+
+A historical `field/PASS` statement about licence position is not a field test;
+a `bench/PASS` measurement extracted from a digital mesh is not a physical bench
+measurement. Keeping such labels active falsely earns T2/T3. Their history must
+remain visible, and a correction must never erase a FAIL or increase trust.
+
+`bin/triad withdraw-positive <ref> --line N --entry-sha256 SHA --reason TEXT
+--artifact PATH --by WHO` appends an `export/CANNOT DETERMINE` row with exactly:
+
+```json
+{"positive_claim_withdrawal":{"line":8,"entry_sha256":"<canonical prior row SHA256>","reason":"why this positive evidence claim is unsupported"}}
+```
+
+The entry hash is SHA256 of canonical UTF-8 JSON (sorted keys, compact separators,
+non-ASCII preserved), excluding only the reader-added `_line`. The command requires
+an existing audit artifact and pins its SHA256. The target must be an earlier,
+exact-hash original PASS row. Missing, forward, self, duplicate, FAIL/CD, wrong-hash
+and reasonless targets are refused before any append. The generic `evidence` extra
+fields cannot bypass this command. The old `retracts/retraction` escape hatch stays
+prohibited.
+
+The original row stays byte-for-byte in the ledger. It is counted and reported as
+**WITHDRAWN POSITIVE CLAIM — historical CANNOT DETERMINE**; its historical artifact
+path is no longer a claim of current evidence. No replacement geometry is implied,
+and a different file must never be relabelled as the missing historical artifact.
+FAIL/CD rows retain all their artifact-integrity and negative-evidence checks.
+
+The command refuses any increase over either computed trust or a lower stored,
+generated trust tier. Only the selected positive contribution is withdrawn;
+negative outcomes remain in the ordinary failure-cap calculation. Invalid/tampered
+correction records produce FAIL findings and a T0 integrity cap; corrupt audit
+provenance must not resurrect the withdrawn physical-trust claim. Corrections and
+their audit hashes are exposed in computed trust.json. This is not a way to assert
+a new measurement, change licence terms, pass geometry or clear a negative test.
